      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MS WICKED SHOWGIRL (8) gets top billing on recent ratings and looks better placed than her finishing positions suggest, with a ninth at Taree still only beaten just over four lengths after looming before being only fair late. She is race fit, has a wet-track placing on the board, and this looks a realistic chance for her to convert that into a win. MOREBAR (2) resumes with solid maiden form, having been fourth at Grafton when near the top of betting and he has placed here and on wet ground, so he has enough substance if ready first-up. ROCKIN' RED (4) is in the mix after missing by a head at Tabulam as a well-supported favourite, although this is a harder assignment and his Wellington run two back was plain. SWEET ENCHANTRESS (10) returns for a new trainer with barrier one and Luke Rolls engaged, and her fifth at Grafton two runs back gives her a genuine placing platform if she resumes in order.",
